  FINDING: No statistically distinguishable difference between dropout
  and no-dropout at alpha=0.05 (p=0.0948, n=5 folds).
  The gated architecture accounts for the bulk of calibration robustness;
  dropout training adds an increment that cannot be resolved at this sample size.
  Framing implication: lead with architecture, not dropout, as the mechanism.

